<%- include('../../partials/header') %>
<style>
:root {
  --primary: #0f766e;
  --primary-hover: #115e59;
  --primary-light: #ccfbf1;
  --slate-900: #0f172a;
  --slate-800: #1e293b;
  --slate-700: #334155;
  --slate-600: #475569;
  --slate-200: #e2e8f0;
  --slate-100: #f1f5f9;
  --slate-50: #f8fafc;
  --white: #ffffff;
  --radius: 16px;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
body { background-color: var(--slate-50); color: var(--slate-800); line-height: 1.6; }
.main-wrapper { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 5rem; }
.page-title-area { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
.page-title-area h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; color: var(--slate-900); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.page-title-area p { color: var(--slate-600); font-size: 1.05rem; }
.calculator-container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
.form-panel { background: var(--white); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--slate-200); box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); }
.results-panel { background: #134e4a; color: #ffffff; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(19,78,74,0.25); }
.section-subtitle { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--slate-600); margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
.input-group { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
.input-group label { display: block; font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--slate-700); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
.input-wrapper { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; }
.input-prefix { position: absolute; left: 1rem; color: var(--slate-600); font-weight: 600; }
.input-suffix { position: absolute; right: 1rem; color: var(--slate-600); font-weight: 600; }
.input-wrapper input, .input-wrapper select {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 2.25rem;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--slate-200);
  border-radius: 10px;
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  outline: none;
  background: #fff;
  transition: border-color 0.2s;
}
.input-wrapper input:focus, .input-wrapper select:focus { border-color: var(--primary); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(15,118,110,0.1); }
.grid-2-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
.comm-hero-card {
  background: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.15);
  border: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.3);
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}
.comm-hero-card .label { font-size: 0.82rem; color: #99f6e4; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; }
.comm-hero-card .val-main { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #5eead4; margin: 0.25rem 0; line-height: 1; }
.comm-hero-card .val-sub { font-size: 0.88rem; color: #ccfbf1; }
.breakdown-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.55rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); }
.breakdown-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.breakdown-row span:first-child { color: #ccfbf1; }
.breakdown-row span:last-child { font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; }
.calculator-content-body { margin-top: 2.5rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding: 2.5rem; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.04); }
.calculator-content-body h2 { font-size: 1.65rem; color: #0f172a; margin: 2rem 0 1rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f5f9; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.calculator-content-body h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; color: #1e293b; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
.calculator-content-body p { color: #475569; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
.calculator-content-body ul, .calculator-content-body ol { margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.75; }
.calculator-content-body li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.table-responsive { overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
.data-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
.data-table th { background: #1e293b; color: #ffffff; padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; font-size: 0.9rem; }
.data-table td { padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9; color: #334155; font-size: 0.92rem; }
.data-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #f8fafc; }
.quick-answer-card { background: #f0fdfa; border-left: 4px solid #0f766e; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
.quick-answer-card h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; color: #115e59; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; border: none; padding: 0; }
.quick-answer-card p { color: #134e4a; margin: 0; }
.faq-item { background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
.faq-item h4 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; color: #0f172a; font-size: 1.05rem; }
.faq-item p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; }
@media (max-width: 860px) {
  .calculator-container { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .grid-2-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
</style>

<main class="main-wrapper">
  <div class="page-title-area">
    <h1>Commercial Real Estate Loan Calculator (<%= currentYear %>)</h1>
    <p>Calculate commercial mortgage payments, balloon balances at maturity, live Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR), Debt Yield, and interest-only amortization schedules.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="calculator-container">
    <div class="form-panel">
      <div class="section-subtitle">1. Property Valuation &amp; Loan Amount</div>
      
      <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commPrice">Property Purchase / Appraised Value</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper">
            <span class="input-prefix">$</span>
            <input type="number" id="commPrice" value="2500000" step="50000">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commLoan">Commercial Loan Amount ($)</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper">
            <span class="input-prefix">$</span>
            <input type="number" id="commLoan" value="1875000" step="25000">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-subtitle" style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">2. Commercial Lending Terms</div>

      <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commRate">Interest Rate (APR %)</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper">
            <input type="number" id="commRate" value="7.25" step="0.125" style="padding-left: 1rem;">
            <span class="input-suffix">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commAmort">Amortization Period</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper" style="padding-left: 0;">
            <select id="commAmort" style="padding-left: 1rem;">
              <option value="30">30 Years (Multifamily / Agency)</option>
              <option value="25" selected>25 Years (Standard Commercial)</option>
              <option value="20">20 Years (Bank Portfolio)</option>
              <option value="15">15 Years (Aggressive)</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commBalloon">Loan Maturity (Balloon Term)</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper" style="padding-left: 0;">
            <select id="commBalloon" style="padding-left: 1rem;">
              <option value="5">5 Years (Standard Bank)</option>
              <option value="7">7 Years (CMBS / Bank)</option>
              <option value="10" selected>10 Years (CMBS / Life Co)</option>
              <option value="15">15 Years</option>
              <option value="25">Fully Amortizing (No Balloon)</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="commIo">Interest-Only Period</label>
          <div class="input-wrapper" style="padding-left: 0;">
            <select id="commIo" style="padding-left: 1rem;">
              <option value="0" selected>0 Years (Amortizing Day 1)</option>
              <option value="1">1 Year Interest-Only</option>
              <option value="2">2 Years Interest-Only</option>
              <option value="3">3 Years Interest-Only</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-subtitle" style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">3. Property Net Operating Income (NOI)</div>
      <div class="input-group">
        <label for="commNoi">Annual Net Operating Income (NOI)</label>
        <div class="input-wrapper">
          <span class="input-prefix">$</span>
          <input type="number" id="commNoi" value="235000" step="5000">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="results-panel">
      <div>
        <div class="comm-hero-card">
          <div class="label">Monthly Debt Service (P&amp;I)</div>
          <div class="val-main" id="resMonthlyPi">$13,554 / mo</div>
          <div class="val-sub" id="resIoLabel">Fully Amortizing 25-Year Schedule</div>
        </div>

        <div class="breakdown-row"><span>Balloon Payment at Maturity:</span><span id="resBalloonAmt" style="color:#fde047;">$1,481,215</span></div>
        <div class="breakdown-row"><span>Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR):</span><span id="resDscr" style="color:#5eead4;">1.44x (Strong)</span></div>
        <div class="breakdown-row"><span>Debt Yield:</span><span id="resDebtYield">12.53%</span></div>
        <div class="breakdown-row"><span>Loan-to-Value (LTV):</span><span id="resLtv">75.0%</span></div>
        <div class="breakdown-row"><span>Total Interest Paid Over Term:</span><span id="resTermInterest">$1,232,711</span></div>
      </div>

      <div style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); padding-top: 1rem; text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #99f6e4;">Initial Required Equity (Down Payment):</div>
        <div style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #5eead4;" id="resEquity">$625,000</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="calculator-content-body">
    <div class="quick-answer-card">
      <h2>Commercial Real Estate Financing Architecture (<%= currentYear %>)</h2>
      <p>Commercial real estate loans differ fundamentally from residential mortgages. Most commercial loans feature <strong>5-, 7-, or 10-year balloon maturities</strong> paired with a <strong>20- to 25-year amortization schedule</strong>. Lenders qualify deals primarily on property performance using <strong>Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR min 1.20x-1.35x)</strong> and <strong>Debt Yield (min 9%-11%)</strong> rather than personal W-2 income.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Commercial Loan Types &amp; Lending Guidelines Matrix</h2>
    <p>Commercial borrowers have multiple capital sources depending on property condition, sponsor experience, and investment horizon:</p>

    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Loan Program</th>
            <th>Max LTV</th>
            <th>Min DSCR</th>
            <th>Term / Amortization</th>
            <th>Recourse Structure</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Bank Portfolio Loan</strong></td><td>65% - 75%</td><td>1.25x - 1.35x</td><td>5-10 Yr Balloon / 20-25 Yr Amort</td><td>Recourse (Personal Guarantee)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>CMBS (Conduit Loan)</strong></td><td>70% - 75%</td><td>1.25x - 1.30x</td><td>5-10 Yr Fixed / 25-30 Yr Amort</td><td>Non-Recourse (Bad Boy Carveouts)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Agency Multifamily (Fannie/Freddie)</strong></td><td>75% - 80%</td><td>1.20x - 1.25x</td><td>5-12 Yr Fixed / 30 Yr Amort</td><td>Non-Recourse</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>SBA 504 (Owner-Occupied)</strong></td><td>Up to 90%</td><td>1.15x - 1.20x</td><td>20-25 Yr Fully Amortizing</td><td>Full Personal Recourse</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Life Insurance Company</strong></td><td>55% - 65%</td><td>1.35x - 1.50x</td><td>10-25 Yr Fixed / 25-30 Yr Amort</td><td>Non-Recourse</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Understanding Balloon Maturity &amp; Refinance Risk</h2>
    <p>Because commercial loans do not fully amortize over their 5- or 10-year maturity periods, the borrower must satisfy the remaining loan principal at the balloon date. For example, an <strong>$1,875,000 commercial mortgage</strong> on a 25-year amortization at 7.25% will still have an unpaid balance of <strong>$1,481,215 at the end of Year 10</strong>.</p>
    
    <h3>3 Strategies to Mitigate Balloon Refinance Risk:</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Drive Net Operating Income (NOI):</strong> Increase tenant rents, reduce operational waste, and maintain low vacancies so the property easily qualifies for replacement financing.</li>
      <li><strong>Monitor Prepayment Windows:</strong> Track your yield maintenance or defeasance lockout expiration dates, and begin negotiating refinance terms 6 to 12 months prior to balloon maturity.</li>
      <li><strong>Maintain Capital Reserves:</strong> Maintain liquidity in case interest rates are higher at maturity, requiring a 'cash-in' refinance to meet lower LTV limits.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>DSCR vs. Debt Yield: How Underwriters Size Loans</h2>
    <p>Commercial lenders evaluate cash flow using two distinct underwriting metrics:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR):</strong> <code>DSCR = Annual NOI / Annual Debt Service (P&amp;I)</code>. A 1.25x DSCR means the property generates $1.25 of net income for every $1.00 of required debt payment.</li>
      <li><strong>Debt Yield:</strong> <code>Debt Yield = (Annual NOI / Total Loan Amount) &times; 100</code>. Unlike DSCR, Debt Yield is interest-rate agnostic and measures the lender's unleveraged return in the event of default. A $235,000 NOI on a $1,875,000 loan represents a strong <strong>12.53% Debt Yield</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>How do commercial real estate balloon loans work?</h4>
      <p>Most commercial loans have a short maturity term (5, 7, or 10 years) with a longer amortization schedule (20 or 25 years). Monthly payments are calculated based on the 25-year schedule, but when the loan term ends, the remaining unpaid balance becomes due immediately in a lump-sum balloon payment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>What DSCR ratio do commercial lenders require in 2026?</h4>
      <p>Most commercial lenders require a minimum DSCR of 1.20x to 1.35x. Prime multifamily properties qualify at 1.20x-1.25x, while hospitality, retail, or suburban office assets often require 1.30x to 1.45x.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>What is Debt Yield in commercial lending and how is it calculated?</h4>
      <p>Debt Yield measures a lender's cash-on-cash return if they had to foreclose: Debt Yield = (Net Operating Income / Loan Amount) × 100. Lenders typically look for a minimum 9.0% to 11.0% Debt Yield.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>What are typical commercial loan interest rates and fees in 2026?</h4>
      <p>Rates typically range from 6.50% to 8.75%. Closing fees include lender origination (0.5%-1.5%), commercial appraisal ($3,500-$7,500), Phase I environmental ($2,000-$3,500), and legal fees ($5,000-$15,000).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>What is the difference between recourse and non-recourse commercial loans?</h4>
      <p>A recourse loan requires a personal guarantee from the borrower, allowing the lender to pursue personal assets upon default. A non-recourse loan restricts lender recovery solely to the property collateral, subject to standard bad-boy carve-outs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>How does commercial loan prepayment work (Defeasance vs Yield Maintenance)?</h4>
      <p>Yield Maintenance requires the borrower to pay the present value of the interest the lender would lose by reinvesting at Treasury rates. Defeasance substitutes real estate collateral with US Treasury bonds generating identical cash flows. Bank loans typically use step-down penalties.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>What maximum LTV can you get on commercial property?</h4>
      <p>Standard commercial banks cap LTV at 65% to 75%. Agency multifamily loans can reach 80% LTV for stabilized apartments, while SBA 504 loans for owner-occupied properties offer up to 90% financing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>How does an interest-only (I/O) period benefit a commercial investor?</h4>
      <p>An interest-only period (1 to 3 years) lowers debt service during initial property stabilization, maximizing cash flow while the sponsor completes renovations, executes tenant lease-ups, and increases NOI.</p>
    </div>

